reims-vgpu: the present capture reuses the render Store's readback.

On the Home screen (~10 presents/s, no host window carrying the
frame): every frame read the compositor's RGBA16F 1206x2622 front (25 MB of
half floats) back from the GPU twice. The render Store read it to land the
guest's pages (store_native_float_surface, native_float_readback_us ~9.4 ms,
native_float_publish_us ~3.5 ms a frame), and the present capture that
followed (capture_resident_bgra_into, reims-present-capture-in-place) read
the same resident again with its own submission and fence to fill the BGRA8
retain the frame mailbox publishes: one more GPU round trip and 25 MB a
frame, 1-2 ms on an idle GPU and 6-10 ms on one another process keeps busy.

Now a native-float Store of a surface a present captured recently, while the
display needs CPU frames, converts the readback it already holds into BGRA8
on its way to the guest (store_capture::stash, through texels_into_bgra, the
conversion half split out of capture_resident_bgra_into so both callers run
the same code), and seals it with the epoch its finish stamped the resident
with. The present capture takes those bytes (store_capture::take, swapped
into the retain without a copy, the old scratch recycled for the next Store)
only when every way the resident could differ from a fresh readback is
excluded:

- same identity (mapping, incarnation, extent, format), and the registry
  slot still names the same VkImage, declared format and extent,
  single-sampled, content-ready, not guest-imported (host-writable memory);
- no queue submission since the readback: a new process-wide count bumped by
  the four DeviceContext entry points that are the only routes to the one
  queue of the one VkDevice, read under the engine lock that covered the
  copy and its fence wait. Equal means the GPU was given nothing since, so no
  rail, with or without registry bookkeeping, can have written the image;
- no recording batch (a fresh readback would append to it and run it first);
- the resident's content stamp and the mapping's surface_content_epoch both
  still at the sealed epoch (a draw recorded into it clears the stamp, a
  guest/host write to the mapping advances the epoch); a Store that failed
  after its readback never seals and its stash is discarded.

Any refusal reads the resident back exactly as before. A stash serves one
present. REIMS_VGPU_STORE_CAPTURE_REUSE=off restores two readbacks a frame.

Census (store_routes): present_capture_reused, present_capture_reused_bytes_n,
present_capture_fresh plus present_capture_fresh_<why> (disabled, nothing,
identity, unsealed, absent, replaced, not_ready, guest_imported,
resident_rewritten, mapping_written, submitted, recording, length);
store_capture_stashed_n, store_capture_convert_us, store_capture_sealed_n,
store_capture_seal_refused_n, store_capture_convert_refused_n,
store_capture_not_presented_n.

Tests: store_capture::tests (verdict: every write shape refused, identity /
seal / length, census names), render_writeback store_capture_gate_tests
(stash only for recently presented surfaces on a CPU display), parity
the_stores_readback_serves_the_present_only_while_nothing_touched_the_resident
(real GPU: reused bytes == in-place capture == copying capture, a draw into
the resident / into another resident / another readback / a moved mapping
epoch / an unsealed stash / another incarnation / another length each force
a fresh readback, and the fresh capture after a rewrite shows the new draw).

