+/// `off` makes every present capture read its resident back from the GPU, the
+/// way each one did before the render Store's readback was reused.
+///
+/// By default a native-float render Store of a surface the display presented
+/// recently converts the bytes it has just read back into BGRA8 on their way to
+/// the guest's pages, tagged with what that readback saw: the resident's
+/// identity, image and extent, and the device's queue-submission count. The
+/// next present capture of that resident takes those bytes instead of reading
+/// the resident a second time, and only when nothing can have changed it since:
+/// no submission and no recording batch, the resident still vouched for at the
+/// epoch the Store sealed, the mapping still at that epoch. Off is a refusal and
+/// never a permission (`present_capture_fresh_disabled`).
+pub const STORE_CAPTURE_REUSE: &str = "REIMS_VGPU_STORE_CAPTURE_REUSE";
+
 /// `off` stages the guest bytes of a `[[buffer(n)]]` bind even when the stage's
